  "narrative": {
    "intro": "L3HARRIS Technologies Integrated Systems L P has $1.1B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. L3HARRIS received 153 awards in the period, with an average award size of $7.2M, and obligations are down 31.2% year over year. Historical obligations show $1.5B in FY21, $1.6B in FY22, $1.5B in FY23, $1.5B in FY24, $1.6B in FY25, and $1.1B in FY26. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer with $1.1B in obligations, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $846K. Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing accounts for $840M of obligations, Aircraft Manufacturing accounts for $149M, and Satellite Telecommunications accounts for $53.1M. Additional markets with recorded obligations include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $40M, Engineering Services at $10.2M, and Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $7.4M. FY2026 totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date reporting.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "L3HARRIS Technologies Integrated Systems L P obligations fell 31.2% year over year for FY2026 to date. L3HARRIS recorded $1.1B in FY26 compared with $1.6B in FY25 and $1.5B in the four prior fiscal years. The FY2026 total is fiscal year to date, so it is a partial-year figure. That partial-year figure is still dominated by Department of Defense obligations of $1.1B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are the biggest markets for L3HARRIS Technologies Integrated Systems L P?",
        "body": "Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing is the largest market at $840M. Aircraft Manufacturing follows at $149M, and Satellite Telecommunications is $53.1M. Secondary markets include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $40M and Engineering Services at $10.2M."
      }
